    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d189">

                <pb facs="0380" n="254" xml:id="pg254"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">121.5760d/2</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Finland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Pearson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Helsingfors</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-02-27"><hi rendition="#italic">February 27,
                        1926</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received March 26.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 149</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to the
                    Department’s circular instruction dated April 2, 1925, regarding the appointment
                    of Customs Attachés.<anchor n="92" xml:id="d189-f1"/></p>
                <p>This matter was taken up with the Finnish Government upon receipt of the
                    Department’s instruction but only a few days ago was a definite reply received
                    to the Legation’s notes. A copy of the reply from the Finnish Foreign Office is
                    enclosed herewith.<anchor n="93" xml:id="d189-f2"/> While the name of Eble alone
                    is mentioned in the reply it is evident that the refusal to accord diplomatic
                    status is intended to include all the Customs Attachés.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alfred J. Pearson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d189-f1" n="92" xml:id="d189-f1-content">
                <p>It was the Department’s instruction No. 133 of May 5 (see footnote 41, <ref
                        target="#pg227">p. 227</ref>), which dealt with the appointment of customs
                    attachés.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d189-f2" n="93" xml:id="d189-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
